# 5. Architectural Principles

## 5.1 Source Independence

Every external source is implemented behind a common connector interface.

```typescript
interface JobSourceConnector {
  discover(): Promise<SourceMetadata>;
  fetchJobs(context: FetchContext): Promise<RawJob[]>;
  normalize(job: RawJob): CanonicalJob;
  healthCheck(): Promise<HealthStatus>;
}
```

Examples:

```text
AdzunaConnector
JoobleConnector
GreenhouseConnector
LeverConnector
AshbyConnector
WorkableConnector
SmartRecruitersConnector
CompanyCareerConnector
GenericCrawlerConnector
```

## 5.2 API First

Preferred order:

```text
Official API
    ↓
Public ATS endpoint
    ↓
Static HTML
    ↓
Headless browser
```

Browser automation is the fallback, not the default.

## 5.3 Event-Driven Processing

Long-running work is asynchronous.

```text
JobDiscovered
      ↓
JobNormalized
      ↓
JobDeduplicated
      ↓
JobMatched
      ↓
ResumeRequested
      ↓
ResumeGenerated
      ↓
ApplicationPrepared
      ↓
HumanApproved
      ↓
ApplicationSubmitted
```

## 5.4 Idempotency

Every ingestion and application operation must be safely repeatable.

Use:

```text
source + sourceJobId
```

where available.

Otherwise:

```text
canonical job fingerprint
```

