# 38. API Idempotency

Mutation endpoints should support idempotency keys where duplicate requests are possible.

Example:

```http
POST /api/applications/123/approve
Idempotency-Key: application-123-approve-v1
```

The same request should not submit an application twice.

---

# 39. Application Double-Submission Protection

Before submission:

```text
Acquire distributed lock
        ↓
Check application status
        ↓
If already submitted → stop
        ↓
Execute application
        ↓
Persist submitted state
        ↓
Release lock
```

Redis distributed locks can be used initially.

