# 53. AI Resume Safety

The AI must not fabricate:

```text
Experience
Employment history
Education
Certifications
Projects
Skills
Achievements
Job titles
Companies
```

It may:

```text
Reorder skills
Emphasize relevant projects
Rewrite truthful descriptions
Improve wording
Change section emphasis
Adapt summary
```

All generated changes should be diffable.

---

# 54. Resume Diff

Before application:

```text
Master Resume
      +
Generated Version
      ↓
Diff Viewer
```

Example:

```diff
- Built web applications using JavaScript.
+ Built React and Next.js web applications using JavaScript,
+ REST APIs, Tailwind CSS and modern frontend architecture.
```

The user can approve or reject changes.

---

# 55. Application Answer Safety

LLM-generated answers must be marked as:

```text
GENERATED
```

until reviewed.

The system should distinguish:

```text
FACTUAL PROFILE DATA
GENERATED CONTENT
USER-APPROVED CONTENT
```

Never allow an LLM to silently overwrite factual candidate data.

---

# 56. Application Form Confidence

Each field mapping gets a confidence level:

```text
HIGH
MEDIUM
LOW
UNKNOWN
```

Example:

```text
Email → candidate.email
confidence: HIGH

Years of experience → candidate.experience
confidence: HIGH

"Tell us about yourself"
confidence: MEDIUM

Unknown custom question
confidence: LOW
```

Low-confidence fields require review.

---

# 57. Browser Execution Safety

Before executing:

```text
Verify target domain
Verify application ID
Verify application status
Verify resume version
Verify required fields
Verify approval
Acquire lock
Execute
Persist events
Release lock
```

This prevents accidental applications to the wrong job or duplicate submissions.

---

# 58. Compliance / Source Policy Layer

Each source gets metadata:

```text
automationAllowed
apiAllowed
crawlAllowed
rateLimit
requiresLogin
requiresManualStep
```

Connector behavior is determined by source policy.

```mermaid
flowchart TD

    SOURCE[Source]
    SOURCE --> POLICY[Policy Resolver]

    POLICY --> ALLOWED{Automation Allowed?}

    ALLOWED -->|Yes| AUTOMATE[Automated Workflow]
    ALLOWED -->|No| ASSIST[Assisted / Manual Workflow]

    ASSIST --> USER[Human]
```

